From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Oct 2026 19:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: report release_object(NULL) rather than faulting.

init_directories() passes the result of every create_*() straight to
release_object(), on the assumption that none can fail. On this console some
do, and the first anyone hears of it is a null dereference inside
release_object, naming neither the creation that failed nor any after it.

Report it with the caller's return address, which identifies the creation, and
return. The startup then continues and every failure is named.
---
diff --git a/server/object.c b/server/object.c
index e977b89480..45f613ec31 100644
--- a/server/object.c
+++ b/server/object.c
@@ -562,6 +562,24 @@ struct object *grab_object( void *ptr )
 /* release an object (i.e. decrement its refcount) */
 void release_object( void *ptr )
 {
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ DIAGNOSTIC. init_directories() passes the result of each create_*()
+     * straight to release_object(), assuming none can fail. On this console
+     * some do, and the null dereference here is the first anyone hears of it --
+     * naming neither the creation that failed nor any after it, because the
+     * server is dead. Report it with the caller's return address, which
+     * identifies the creation, and carry on. */
+    if (!ptr)
+    {
+        extern int sceKernelDebugOutText( int channel, const char *text );
+        char line[160];
+        snprintf( line, sizeof(line),
+                  "wineserver: release_object(NULL) from %p -- a create_* call failed\n",
+                  __builtin_return_address(0) );
+        sceKernelDebugOutText( 0, line );
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
     struct object *obj = (struct object *)ptr;
     assert( obj->refcount );
     if (!--obj->refcount)
